### Context: Task 2.7 – Calendar Generation Service Implementation (from .codemachine/artifacts/plan/02_Iteration_I2.md)

```markdown
<!-- anchor: task-i2-t7 -->
**Task 2.7: Calendar Generation Service Implementation**

- **Task ID:** `I2.T7`
- **Description:** Implement core calendar generation logic using existing codebase from main app (astronomical calculations via SunCalc, Proj4J; PDF rendering via Apache PDFBox and Batik). Create service that accepts UserCalendar entity, renders calendar with template configuration, generates PDF, uploads to Cloudflare R2, returns URL. This extracts and refactors existing calendar generation code into standalone service.
- **Agent Type Hint:** `BackendAgent`
- **Inputs:**
  - Existing calendar generation code in main app (if any - spec mentions CalendarTemplate entity exists)
  - Apache PDFBox documentation (PDF creation)
  - Apache Batik documentation (SVG rendering)
  - SunCalc library documentation (astronomical events)
  - Cloudflare R2 S3-compatible API
- **Input Files:**
  - `VillageCMS/admin/src/main/java/villagecompute/vc/services/CalendarService.java` (if exists in main app)
  - `village-calendar/src/main/java/com/villagecompute/calendar/data/UserCalendar.java` (from I2.T2)
  - `village-calendar/src/main/java/com/villagecompute/calendar/data/CalendarTemplate.java` (from I2.T2)
- **Target Files:**
